Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add NVLink Engram fetch for single-node runs without NCCL
 GIN

DeepEP's EngramBuffer only implements fetch via NCCL GIN (GPU-initiated
RDMA), so V4.1 crashes with an illegal address on single-node machines
whose RDMA NICs are unusable, even though EP and DeepGEMM work over NVLink.

Add NVLinkEngramBuffer, a drop-in for the write/fetch/destroy subset used
by EngramRuntime: indices are all-gathered, each rank looks up the rows it
owns, and one all_to_all returns them. Buffers are padded to
max_num_tokens, so there is no host sync and it is CUDA-graph capturable.

Enable with DEEPINFER_ENGRAM_NVLINK_FETCH=1; it defaults on when
EP_DISABLE_GIN=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
